# The stress-test meeting: (speaker, language, text). G = Guillaume (mic), S = Sarah (producer),
# M = Marc (lead programmer) — S and M are the remote participants.
SCRIPT = [
("G", "en", "Okay, I think everyone is here. Thanks for joining. So the goal today is simple: we need to decide which engine we use for Skyward Tales 2, because the pre-production starts in January and we can't keep postponing this."),
("S", "en", "Yes, and the publisher asked me again on Monday. They want a first playable build in June, and the full release is still planned for the fourth quarter of 2027, on PC, PlayStation 5 and Switch 2."),
("M", "en", "Before we start, I want to say that I wrote a short document with the four options. Staying on Unity, moving to Unreal Engine 5, switching to Godot 4, or building our own engine. I sent it this morning."),
("G", "en", "Great, I read it on the train. Let's go through them one by one. Marc, can you start with Unity, since that's what we used for the first game?"),
("M", "en", "Sure. The big advantage is obvious: the whole team knows Unity and C sharp. We have three years of tools, editor scripts and a custom character controller. If we stay, we can start producing content on day one."),
("M", "en", "The problems are also known. The runtime fee story in 2023 hurt the trust a lot, even if they cancelled it. And the Pro licenses went up again, we pay around two thousand two hundred dollars per seat per year now."),
("S", "en", "With fourteen people on the team that's about thirty thousand dollars a year, just for the licenses. It's not nothing, but compared to salaries it's still small. My real worry is the risk that they change the rules again in the middle of our production."),
("G", "en", "Right. And performance on Switch 2? The first game was really difficult to optimize on the Switch."),
("M", "en", "Unity 6 is better, the new render pipeline helps. But honestly, we had to fight the garbage collector for months. On Switch 2 it should be easier because the hardware is much stronger, but I wouldn't say the problem is solved."),
("G", "en", "Okay. Unreal next."),
("M", "en", "Unreal 5 is the most powerful option on paper. Nanite and Lumen, very good tools for open worlds, and console support is excellent because every big studio uses it. The royalty is five percent of gross revenue above one million dollars per product."),
("S", "en", "For the first game we made around four million dollars in revenue. So with Unreal we would have paid around one hundred and fifty thousand dollars. That's more than five years of Unity licenses."),
("M", "en", "Yes. And the other cost is people. Nobody here really knows C plus plus at the level Unreal needs, except me and maybe Julie. We would need to hire at least two senior engine programmers, and they are expensive and hard to find in Lyon."),
("G", "en", "And our art style is cartoon, not photorealistic. Do we even need Nanite and Lumen?"),
("M", "en", "Not really. That's my point. Unreal is amazing for realistic games, but for a stylized co-op adventure we would pay for a lot of features we don't use, and the builds are huge. A small patch on Switch could be several gigabytes."),
("S", "en", "So Unreal is basically too expensive for what we need. I would put it at the bottom of the list, unless the publisher pushes for it."),
("G", "en", "I agree. Let's keep it as a fallback but not invest time in it. Now Godot."),
("M", "en", "Godot 4 is the one I'm most excited about. It's open source under the MIT license, so no royalties and no license fees, ever. Nobody can change the rules. The editor is light, it starts in two seconds, and the 2D and 3D tools improved a lot in version 4.3 and 4.4."),
("M", "en", "The script language GDScript is easy, and Godot also supports C sharp, so part of our code could be ported instead of rewritten. I did a small test last week with our camera code and it took me one afternoon."),
("G", "en", "What about consoles? That was always the weak point of Godot."),
("M", "en", "Yes, that's the main risk. Godot itself can't ship console code publicly because of the console NDAs. You go through a company like W4 Games, which provides official ports for PlayStation, Xbox and Switch. I don't know their prices yet."),
("S", "en", "I can contact them. I met someone from W4 at Gamescom. I'll ask for a quote for PS5 and Switch 2, and also what support they include."),
("G", "en", "Perfect, thanks Sarah. Can you try to get an answer by next Friday?"),
("S", "en", "Yes, I'll write to them today and I'll get back to you by Friday the 31st."),
("M", "en", "The other risk with Godot is the ecosystem. On Unity we buy plugins for everything. On Godot there are fewer assets, so some things we would have to build ourselves, especially the networking for the co-op mode."),
("G", "en", "How long would the netcode take?"),
("M", "en", "Godot has high level multiplayer built in, but for four players online with rollback I think we need something more solid. Maybe two to three months for one person. On Unity we used Netcode for GameObjects and it was already painful."),
("G", "en", "Okay. And the last option, our own engine. I know some people in the team really want that."),
("M", "en", "I'm one of them, to be honest. Full control, no license, we optimize exactly for our game. But I did the estimate and it's at least eighteen to twenty-four months before artists can work comfortably, with three engine programmers full time."),
("S", "en", "That's impossible with our timeline. First playable in June means we need to produce content from February. A custom engine would push the release to 2029."),
("M", "en", "I know. I'm not proposing it for Skyward Tales 2. Maybe for the game after, if we start building small parts of it now, like our own tools for dialogue and quests that don't depend on the engine."),
("G", "en", "I like that idea. Engine independent tools that we can keep whatever we choose. Let's note it as an idea for later, not a decision."),
("S", "en", "So if I summarize: custom engine is out for this game, Unreal is a fallback, and the real choice is between staying on Unity and moving to Godot."),
("G", "en", "Exactly. Marc, what would you need to compare them seriously?"),
("M", "en", "I would build the same small vertical slice in both engines. The traversal, one combat encounter, and two players in co-op over the network. Two weeks for Godot, because I need to learn some parts, and a few days in Unity 6 to measure the difference with our current version."),
("G", "en", "Two weeks is fine. Can you have both prototypes ready by November 14?"),
("M", "en", "November 14 works if Julie can help me with the netcode part. I'll ask her today."),
("S", "en", "And I need numbers for the publisher. Guillaume, can you prepare the cost comparison over three years? Licenses, hiring, training and console ports for each option."),
("G", "en", "Yes, I'll do the spreadsheet. I'll have a first version before the prototypes are done, let's say November 10, and I'll update it with the W4 quote when we have it."),
("S", "en", "Good. Then I suggest we take the final decision on November 20, with the whole team, after we play both prototypes."),
("G", "en", "Agreed, November 20 for the decision. I'll send the invitation."),
("M", "en", "One more thing about the asset pipeline. Our characters and levels are Unity prefabs. Moving them to Godot means converting everything, and the shaders have to be rewritten. I think the shaders are maybe three weeks for our technical artist."),
("S", "en", "Is that included in your estimate for the migration?"),
("M", "en", "Not yet. Good point. I'll add the asset and shader migration to the document so we see the full cost."),
("G", "en", "Also the Switch 2 dev kits. Do we have a date?"),
("S", "en", "No, Nintendo said maybe December, but nothing official. That's an open question, it affects the performance tests for both engines."),
('G', 'en', "Before we move on, let's talk a bit about the scope of the release itself, because the engine choice depends on what we want to build. Sarah, where are we with the feature list?"),
('S', 'en', 'The publisher validated four big features. Four player co-op instead of two, a new desert biome, cross-play between PC and consoles, and a photo mode. They also asked about mod support, but that one is not validated yet.'),
('M', 'en', "Four players is the hardest one technically. It doubles the network traffic and the number of characters on screen. On Switch 2 that's where we'll see if the engine holds or not."),
('G', 'en', 'And cross-play? Is that a big problem with Godot?'),
('M', 'en', "Cross-play itself is more about the online services than the engine. We would use something like Epic Online Services or Steam networking, and they work with any engine through their SDK. With Godot we need a plugin, there's a community one, but I haven't tested it."),
('S', 'en', 'Can you add that to the prototype? Even a very simple lobby with two platforms?'),
('M', 'en', "Not in two weeks, sorry. I can test that the plugin compiles and connects, but a real cross-play lobby is more work. Let's keep it as a risk for now."),
('G', 'en', "Okay, that's fair. Let's write it down as a risk. What about mod support? I know the community asked a lot for it after the first game."),
('M', 'en', "That's actually a strong argument for Godot. Because the engine is open source, modders can use the same editor as us. With Unity, mod support always means building a special SDK, and with Unreal it's possible but very heavy."),
('S', 'en', 'But mods also mean moderation, legal questions, and support. Sony and Nintendo have strict rules for user content on consoles. I would limit mods to PC at first.'),
('G', 'en', "I agree, mods on PC only, and probably after launch, not for day one. Let's not add work to the release."),
('S', 'en', "Good. I'll tell the publisher that mod support is a post launch feature, PC only."),
('G', 'en', 'Now another topic Marc wanted to mention: the build pipeline. Our builds are really slow today.'),
('M', 'en', "Yes. A full Unity build for Switch takes about forty minutes on our build machine, and for PlayStation it's almost an hour. The artists wait for the nightly build every time. In Godot, my test project exported in less than two minutes, but of course it's much smaller."),
('G', 'en', 'That would change our daily work a lot. Can you measure the export time on the prototype too, with the same assets in both engines?'),
('M', 'en', "Yes, I'll measure the export time on both. That's easy to add."),
('S', 'en', 'And the demo for Steam Next Fest? The publisher would like a public demo in June, at the same time as the first playable.'),
('G', 'en', "June is very tight if we change engine. Honestly, if we go with Godot, I'd rather show a trailer in June and a demo in October."),
('S', 'en', "The publisher won't like that. The June Next Fest is important for wishlists. For the first game, the demo brought almost forty percent of our wishlists before launch."),
('M', 'en', "Then it's another argument for Unity, at least for the demo. We could build the demo in Unity and migrate after. But that would be double work, I don't recommend it."),
('G', 'en', "No, double work is the worst option. Let's say the demo date depends on the engine decision, and Sarah discusses it with the publisher after November 20."),
('S', 'en', "Okay, I'll keep the demo question open until then."),
('G', 'en', 'And localization? We had twelve languages for the first game.'),
('S', 'en', "Same for the second one, plus Korean. Unity has the localization package we already use. For Godot there's a built-in translation system with CSV or gettext files, which is actually what our translation agency prefers."),
('M', 'en', "Yes, Godot's translation system is good. Fonts for Asian languages need some care, but nothing blocking."),
("G", "en", "Okay. Let's switch to French for the second part, Marc wants to discuss the team side and I think it's easier for everyone."),
("M", "fr", "Oui merci, ce sera plus simple pour moi. Alors, le vrai sujet pour moi c'est l'équipe. Si on passe sur Godot, il faut former tout le monde, et je ne veux pas qu'on perde la motivation des gens au milieu de la préproduction."),
("S", "fr", "Je suis d'accord. Moi j'ai fait un petit sondage la semaine dernière. Sur quatorze personnes, neuf sont plutôt pour essayer Godot, trois préfèrent rester sur Unity, et deux n'ont pas d'avis."),
("G", "fr", "C'est intéressant, je ne pensais pas qu'il y aurait autant de monde pour Godot. Les trois qui veulent rester sur Unity, ce sont surtout les artistes ?"),
("S", "fr", "Oui, surtout les artistes et le level designer. Ils ont peur de perdre leurs outils, notamment l'éditeur de niveaux qu'on a fait nous-mêmes dans Unity."),
("M", "fr", "Ça c'est un vrai point. Notre éditeur de niveaux, c'est six mois de travail. Il faudrait le refaire dans Godot. Je pense qu'on peut en refaire une version simple en un mois, mais pas toutes les fonctionnalités."),
("G", "fr", "Est-ce qu'on pourrait demander aux artistes de tester le prototype Godot aussi, pas seulement les programmeurs ?"),
("M", "fr", "Oui, bonne idée. Je peux préparer une petite scène pour eux, avec l'import d'un personnage et d'un décor. Comme ça ils voient concrètement à quoi ressemble le travail."),
("S", "fr", "Et pour la formation, j'ai regardé les prix. Il y a une formation Godot en ligne pour toute l'équipe à environ cinq mille euros, sur trois semaines, avec un formateur qui a déjà sorti des jeux sur console."),
("G", "fr", "Cinq mille euros c'est raisonnable. On a ce budget ?"),
("S", "fr", "Oui, on a un budget formation de douze mille euros pour l'année prochaine, et presque rien n'est utilisé. Je peux bloquer les cinq mille dès maintenant, comme ça si on choisit Godot on peut commencer en janvier."),
("G", "fr", "D'accord, on bloque le budget formation, c'est décidé. Si on reste sur Unity, on l'utilisera pour autre chose."),
("M", "fr", "Par contre, il y a un sujet que je veux qu'on ne sous-estime pas, c'est le recrutement. Si on choisit Godot, il y a moins de développeurs expérimentés sur le marché. Il faudra peut-être former des gens qui viennent de Unity."),
("S", "fr", "Moi je pense que c'est plutôt une chance. Beaucoup de développeurs Unity veulent quitter Unity depuis l'histoire du runtime fee. Si on dit qu'on fait du Godot, ça peut attirer des gens."),
("G", "fr", "C'est vrai, et ça peut aussi nous faire une bonne communication. Un studio français qui sort un jeu console sur Godot, ça intéresse la presse."),
("M", "fr", "Oui, mais attention, on ne choisit pas un moteur pour la communication. Si le jeu tourne mal sur Switch, la presse en parlera aussi."),
("G", "fr", "Tu as raison. La performance sur Switch 2 reste le critère numéro un. Si le prototype Godot ne tient pas soixante images par seconde en coopération à deux joueurs, on reste sur Unity."),
("S", "fr", "Donc on fixe des critères clairs pour le vingt novembre. Je propose : performance sur console, temps de production pour les artistes, coût sur trois ans, et risque sur le planning."),
("M", "fr", "Et j'ajoute la qualité du réseau en coopération, parce que c'est le cœur du jeu."),
("G", "fr", "Parfait, cinq critères. Sarah, tu peux les mettre dans un document partagé avant la réunion, avec une note de un à cinq pour chaque moteur ?"),
("S", "fr", "Oui, je fais ça. Je l'envoie à tout le monde le dix-sept novembre, comme ça chacun a le temps de le lire avant la décision."),
("M", "fr", "Il reste une question que je n'ai pas tranchée : est-ce qu'on garde le C sharp dans Godot ou est-ce qu'on passe tout en GDScript ? Le C sharp dans Godot ne marche pas encore partout sur console."),
("G", "fr", "Ça, on ne peut pas décider aujourd'hui. Il faut la réponse de W4 sur le support du C sharp sur PS5 et Switch 2."),
("S", "fr", "Je l'ajoute à mes questions pour W4."),
("M", "fr", "Dernier point de mon côté : je voudrais qu'on commence dès maintenant les outils indépendants du moteur dont on parlait, pour les dialogues et les quêtes. Ce sera utile quel que soit le choix."),
("G", "fr", "Oui, je suis pour. Mais seulement après les prototypes, je ne veux pas que ça te retarde. On en reparle après le vingt novembre."),
("S", "fr", "Et il faut prévenir l'éditeur. Je lui écris pour lui dire qu'on prendra la décision le vingt novembre et qu'on lui envoie une estimation du planning juste après."),
('G', 'fr', "Avant de conclure, je voudrais qu'on regarde le planning mois par mois, pour voir où est le risque si on change de moteur."),
('S', 'fr', "Alors, voilà ce que j'ai. Novembre, les prototypes et la décision. Décembre, la formation si on part sur Godot, et la migration des outils. Janvier et février, la préproduction avec le premier niveau du désert. Mars à mai, la production du contenu pour la première version jouable. Et juin, la version jouable pour l'éditeur."),
('M', 'fr', "Le problème c'est décembre. Julie part en congé paternité le quinze décembre pour deux mois, et c'est elle qui connaît le mieux le réseau. Si on change de moteur, on la perd au pire moment."),
('G', 'fr', "Ah, je n'avais pas ça en tête. Est-ce qu'elle pourrait documenter la partie réseau avant de partir ?"),
('M', 'fr', "Oui, je vais lui demander de préparer une documentation du code réseau et de former quelqu'un d'autre avant le quinze décembre. Je pense à Thomas, il est motivé."),
('S', 'fr', "C'est un vrai risque, il faut le noter. Si le réseau prend du retard, toute la coopération à quatre joueurs prend du retard."),
('G', 'fr', "D'accord. Et si on reste sur Unity, le planning est plus simple ?"),
('S', 'fr', "Oui, on gagne environ un mois et demi. Pas de formation, pas de migration d'outils. Mais on garde le risque sur les licences et sur les performances Switch."),
('M', 'fr', "Moi je préfère perdre un mois et demi maintenant que six mois à la fin à optimiser pour la Switch. Sur le premier jeu, l'optimisation nous a coûté presque tout l'été."),
('G', 'fr', "Je comprends. C'est pour ça que le prototype sur console est si important. Est-ce qu'on a au moins un kit de développement Switch 1 pour tester en attendant ?"),
('M', 'fr', "Oui, on a encore deux kits Switch 1. Ce n'est pas la même puissance, mais si le prototype tourne bien sur Switch 1, il tournera sur Switch 2. Je peux faire le test dessus."),
('G', 'fr', 'Très bien, fais le test sur le kit Switch 1, ça nous donnera une première idée.'),
('S', 'fr', "Il faut aussi penser à la QA. Pour le premier jeu, on avait externalisé les tests console chez un prestataire à Montréal. Ils m'ont demandé si on continue avec eux."),
('G', 'fr', 'Ils étaient bons ?'),
('S', 'fr', "Très bons sur PlayStation, un peu moins sur Switch. Et ils n'ont jamais testé de jeu Godot, donc il faudra leur demander s'ils sont à l'aise avec ça."),
('M', 'fr', 'Pour la QA, le moteur change surtout les outils de rapport de bugs et de crash. Sur Godot il faudra intégrer un outil comme Sentry ou BugSplat nous-mêmes.'),
('G', 'fr', "D'accord. Sarah, tu peux leur poser la question, sans engagement pour l'instant ?"),
('S', 'fr', 'Oui, je leur écris la semaine prochaine.'),
('G', 'fr', "Dernière chose avant le résumé : la communication à l'équipe. Je ne veux pas que les gens apprennent la décision par une rumeur."),
('S', 'fr', "Je propose qu'on fasse une réunion de toute l'équipe ce vendredi, pour expliquer le processus : les prototypes, les critères, et la date du vingt novembre. Comme ça tout le monde sait comment on va décider."),
('M', 'fr', "Bonne idée. Et je peux présenter rapidement le prototype Godot de la caméra, pour montrer que ce n'est pas un saut dans le vide."),
('G', 'fr', "Parfait. Réunion d'équipe vendredi à seize heures, Sarah présente le processus et Marc fait une démo de cinq minutes."),
("G", "fr", "Très bien. Je résume rapidement. Marc fait les deux prototypes pour le quatorze novembre avec l'aide de Julie, et une scène de test pour les artistes. Sarah contacte W4 Games pour un devis d'ici le trente et un octobre, prépare la grille des critères pour le dix-sept, et prévient l'éditeur."),
("G", "fr", "Moi je fais le tableau des coûts pour le dix novembre, et j'envoie l'invitation pour la réunion de décision du vingt novembre. On a décidé d'abandonner le moteur maison pour ce jeu, de garder Unreal en plan de secours, et de bloquer cinq mille euros pour la formation."),
("M", "fr", "C'est clair pour moi. Et n'oublie pas la migration des shaders dans ton tableau, c'est trois semaines pour notre technical artist."),
("G", "fr", "Oui, je l'ajoute. Merci à tous, bonne fin de journée."),
("S", "fr", "Merci, à bientôt."),
]
